From 6d605f4246b4e52c0399abd30b2b3c0263396e95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 03:23:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02240/11362] [outer-loop] wire E3 into agent (offline-legal
 pluggable proposer) + focused-loop eval engine

KEY ARCHITECTURE CORRECTION: the competition eval is OFFLINE (no internet), so codex/
gpt-5.5 (closed, online) CANNOT be the engine there. E3 proposer is now PLUGGABLE:
- LocalGGUFProposer (open gemma-4 GGUF via llama.cpp, OFFLINE) = the competition-legal,
  decentralized default (CLAUDE.md decentralization rule 1-2).
- CodexProposer marked offline_legal=False (DEV-ONLY, validates the loop with internet).
E3AgentPolicy wires the strong choose_action: explore->collect transitions->induce(local
proposer)->VERIFY(Carnot verifier)->plan->execute. Verifier grounds the model regardless
of model strength.

scripts/arc_leaderboard_eval.py = the focused-loop measurement engine: scores the agent
FROM SCRATCH with the leaderboard metric (levels + min(human/agent,1)^2) on the public
games + logs which games fail (gap log) so each iteration targets the worst gap. Baseline:
2 levels (lp85 eff 1.0, sp80), 9 open gaps. NOTE: we use NEITHER TRM nor a closed
foundation model in the core explorer (training-free graph search); E3's engine is an
OPEN LOCAL model. TRM (Sudoku-trained) is NOT on the ARC-AGI-3 path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
